From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Velez Garcia <velezgarciaemmanuel25@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 14:36:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add p99, an "other" section, and spike logging

Three gaps in the measurement, all of them things that have to exist
before an optimisation can be justified rather than assumed.

p99 sits next to p95. They answer different questions: p95 is how the
server feels most of the time, p99 is how often it stutters, and a server
can hold a good p95 while one tick in a hundred is terrible.

"Other" is the part of the average tick the sections do not cover - the
network tick, the player list, tickables, and plugins inside Bukkit
events. It was previously visible only on the worst tick, so the averages
silently did not add up to the MSPT above them. A large "other" is where
to look next, which is worth showing rather than hiding.

Spike logging writes a tick over debug.logTickSpikesOverMs to the log
with its breakdown, as it happens. /vs perf reports the worst tick of the
last minute, but only when somebody runs it - a spike at four in the
morning is gone by the time anyone reads about it. Rate limited by
debug.spikeLogIntervalTicks, because a struggling server spikes every
tick and a line for each turns a performance problem into a disk problem.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/com/voidsoul/spigot/config/VoidSoulConfig.java b/src/main/java/com/voidsoul/spigot/config/VoidSoulConfig.java
